      "updated_at": "2018-05-21T11:41:28Z",
      "body": "You can just try to remove the addEventListener if you put this code at the bottom of the `<body>` block, eg:\r\n```html\r\n(function() {\r\n  ...\r\n})();\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd also, you can use `window.pageLoad` to handle the callback, even the `load` event has been emitted, the callback would still working:\r\n```\r\nwindow.pageLoad.then(function() {\r\n  ...\r\n});\r\n```\r\nYou can see the source [here](https://github.com/kitian616/jekyll-TeXt-theme/blob/master/_includes/scripts/utils.js#L17)",
